 "exercises": [
  {
   "id": "cp1",
   "source_id": "fs-id1167794031036",
   "source_number": "Checkpoint 11.4",
   "kind": "checkpoint",
   "bloom": "Apply",
   "place": {
    "at": "inline",
    "after": "fs-id1167793984213"
   },
   "cite": "fs-id1167793898113",
   "prompt": "<p>Calculate the derivative $dy/dx$ for the plane curve defined by the equations</p>\n$$x(t)=t^{2}-4t,\\;y(t)=2t^{3}-6t,\\;-2\\le t\\le 3$$\n<p>and locate any critical points on its graph.</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
    "generated_by": "source",
    "solution": "<p>$x^{\\prime}(t)=2t-4$ and $y^{\\prime}(t)=6t^{2}-6,$ so $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{6t^{2}-6}{2t-4}=\\frac{3t^{2}-3}{t-2}.$</p>\n<p>This expression is undefined when $t=2$ and equal to zero when $t=±1.$</p>\n<img src=\"/media/ch11/CNX_Calc_Figure_11_02_005.jpg\" alt=\"A curve going from (12, −4) through the origin and (−4, 0) to (−3, 36) with arrows in that order. The point (12, −4) is marked t = −2 and the point (−3, 36) is marked t = 3. On the graph there are also written three equations: x(t) = t2 – 4t, y(t) = 2t3 – 6t, and −2 ≤ t ≤ 3.\">",
    "hint": "Calculate $x^{\\prime}(t)$ and $y^{\\prime}(t)$ and use <a href=\"#fs-id1167793881791\">Equation 11.1</a>."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "cp2",
   "source_id": "fs-id1167794011461",
   "source_number": "Checkpoint 11.5",
   "kind": "checkpoint",
   "bloom": "Apply",
   "place": {
    "at": "inline",
    "after": "fs-id1167794042393"
   },
   "cite": "fs-id1167793898113",
   "prompt": "<p>Find an equation of the tangent line to the curve defined by the equations</p>\n$$x(t)=t^{2}-4t,\\;y(t)=2t^{3}-6t,\\;-2\\le t\\le 10\\;\\text{when}\\;t=5.$$",
   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
    "generated_by": "source",
    "solution": "The equation of the tangent line is $y=24x+100.$",
    "hint": "Calculate $x^{\\prime}(t)$ and $y^{\\prime}(t)$ and use <a href=\"#fs-id1167793881791\">Equation 11.1</a>."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "cp3",
   "source_id": "fs-id1167793984347",
   "source_number": "Checkpoint 11.6",
   "kind": "checkpoint",
   "bloom": "Apply",
   "place": {
    "at": "inline",
    "after": "fs-id1167794044408"
   },
   "cite": "second-order",
   "prompt": "<p>Calculate the second derivative $d^{2}y/dx^{2}$ for the plane curve defined by the equations</p>\n$$x(t)=t^{2}-4t,\\;y(t)=2t^{3}-6t,\\;-2\\le t\\le 3$$\n<p>and locate any critical points on its graph.</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
    "generated_by": "source",
    "solution": "$\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}}=\\frac{3t^{2}-12t+3}{2{(t-2)}^{3}}.$ Critical points $(5,4),(-3,-4),\\text{and}\\;(-4,4).$",
    "hint": "Start with the solution from the previous checkpoint, and use <a href=\"#fs-id1167794072159\">Equation 11.2</a>."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "cp4",
   "source_id": "fs-id1167794074320",
   "source_number": "Checkpoint 11.7",
   "kind": "checkpoint",
   "bloom": "Apply",
   "place": {
    "at": "inline",
    "after": "fs-id1167794038444"
   },
   "cite": "fs-id1167794038315",
   "prompt": "<p>Find the area under the curve of the hypocycloid defined by the equations</p>\n$$x(t)=3\\;\\cos t+\\cos 3t,\\;y(t)=3\\;\\sin t-\\sin 3t,\\;0\\le t\\le \\pi .$$",
   "answer": {
    "type": "number",
    "generated_by": "source",
    "value": 9.42477796076938,
    "tol": 0.01,
    "solution": "$A=3\\pi$ (Note that the integral formula actually yields a negative answer. This is due to the fact that $x(t)$ is a decreasing function over the interval $[0,2\\pi ];$<sup class=\"fn\" data-note=\"c-cp7-interval\"></sup> that is, the curve is traced from right to left.)",
    "hint": "Use <a href=\"#fs-id1167794038394\">Equation 11.3</a>, along with the identities $\\sin \\alpha \\;\\sin β=\\frac{1}{2}[\\cos (\\alpha -β)-\\cos (\\alpha +β)]$ and ${\\sin }^{2}t=\\frac{1-\\cos 2t}{2}.$"
   }
  },
  {
